Z||000012||Capt Fiero||10-04-2001||10:23 AM||||I was really thinking about going NOS, and had even started getting parts ready for it, and once again I have changed my mind.  HeHe.  Well I have priced out the main parts I am going to need.  I have an 85 V6 ECM that will accept the Knock Sensor so I am good there. Here is what I am looking at for Prices in Cdn $$.<P>Knock Sensor single wire GM 60$<BR>2-Bar Map Sensor Delco 80$<BR>Turbo good used with warrenty from wrecker 200$<BR>Y-pipe raw matirels with turbo flanges 100$<BR>Friend to weld and set up new Y-Pipe 100$ more. Y-Pipe total about 200$  <BR>Oil Feed lines and  misc stuff 60$<BR>Turbo pipes to go from turbo to intake and air box to turbo plus other misc. 50$<P><BR>Total Cost for a home built turbo is 650$<P>The important stuff I already have, Full MSD Ignition, 6A box and all the good stuff.  19# injectors, motor has been rebuilt with Chrom-Moly Rings.  I have too much to list in small stuff done to the motor, but it should make for an interesting turbo application.  If anyone else has any comments please feel free. To email me at hotrodfiero@shaw.ca or post here.<P>When I compare this to a NOS kit the price is close and I will always have it there, plus no bottle refils.  <P>||||reg||1
